Case 1: hash-join by cost without a hint - inner, left outer and right outer join     

===================================================
count(*)    sum(a.id)    sum(b.id)    
80000     800040000     800040000     

Query plan:
hash-join (inner join)
    edge:  term[?]
    outer: sscan
               class: a node[?]
               cost:  ? card ?
    inner: sscan
               class: b node[?]
               cost:  ? card ?
    cost:  ? card ?
Query stmt:
select count(*), sum(a.id), sum(b.id) from t_big? a, t_big? b where a.k=b.k
===================================================
count(*)    sum(a.id)    sum(b.id)    count(b.id)    
40000     400020000     600020000     40000     

Query plan:
hash-join (left outer join)
    edge:  term[?]
    outer: sscan
               class: a node[?]
               cost:  ? card ?
    inner: sscan
               class: b node[?]
               sargs: term[?]
               cost:  ? card ?
    cost:  ? card ?
Query stmt:
select count(*), sum(a.id), sum(b.id), count(b.id) from t_big? a left outer join t_big? b on (b.id> ?:? ) and a.k=b.k
===================================================
count(*)    sum(a.id)    sum(b.id)    count(a.id)    
40000     600020000     400020000     40000     

Query plan:
hash-join (right outer join)
    edge:  term[?]
    outer: sscan
